# The mobile app is a separate project living inside this repository. Its native
# packaging shells are ~5GB and none of it belongs in the service image, yet the
# bare `node_modules`/`dist` patterns above only match the repository root — so
# the whole directory was being shipped as Docker build context.
HDdaraAi

# Local-only state and secrets.
.codebuddy_data
.codebuddy_creds
.brv

# Development-time files that must never ship.
#
# `next build` writes the project root into `.next/standalone`, and the runner
# stage copies that directory wholesale — so anything left out of this file ends
# up inside the production image. Verified by pulling the published image:
# `.env` (local values) and `.mcp.json` (a Grafana service-account token plus
# GitHub and docker-swarm auth headers) were both in there.
.env
.env.*
.mcp.json
.codebuddy
.agents
.github
.husky
.vscode
.playwright-mcp
AGENTS.md
